THOUGHT: The new NullAway errors are: (1) HttpRequestBuilder.httpRequest is a non-null field that’s set to null and not initialized in the constructor; (2) NetJavaImpl uses a possibly-null method string; (3) NetJavaServerSocketImpl dereferences possibly-null server. I’ll fix them minimally: make httpRequest @Nullable so assigning null and checking for null is valid; in NetJavaImpl, guard uses of method with a null check and throw if null; in NetJavaServerSocketImpl, ensure server is non-null before accept() by throwing if it’s null. Then I’ll rebuild to confirm the total error count is now 451 (one less than the original 452 after the first fix) and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '52s/private HttpRequest httpRequest;/@Nullable private HttpRequest httpRequest;/' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/net/HttpRequestBuilder.java && sed -i '171,182s/^/      /' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/net/NetJavaImpl.java && sed -i '171s/final String method = httpRequest.getMethod();/final String method = httpRequest.getMethod();
      if (method == null) {
        throw new GdxRuntimeException("HTTP method cannot be null");
      }/' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/net/NetJavaImpl.java && sed -i '83s/return new NetJavaSocketImpl(server.accept(), hints);/if (server == null) {
        throw new GdxRuntimeException("Server socket is not initialized");
      }
      return new NetJavaSocketImpl(server.accept(), hints);/' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/net/NetJavaServerSocketImpl.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && tail -n 40 new_build_output.log
```

